sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Administrator
    participant IdP as Identity Provider<br/>(Keycloak / Okta / etc.)
    participant GrantTool as polar-admin-grant<br/>(holds its own Polar cert --<br/>see admin_bootstrap_identity.mmd)
    participant Cassini as Cassini broker
    participant CredAgentCon as Credentials Agent<br/>(consumer -- high trust)
    participant EventLog as Event log<br/>(hash-chained JSONL,<br/>PersistentVolume-backed --<br/>the actual record of truth)
    participant Graph as Neo4j<br/>(rebuildable projection --<br/>observability only)

    Note over Admin,Graph: Phase 0 -- Admin provisions the user in the IdP<br/>(may already exist -- shown for completeness)

    Admin->>IdP: Provision user account<br/>(or confirm an existing one)
    activate IdP
    IdP-->>Admin: Account created/confirmed
    deactivate IdP

    Admin->>IdP: Query the account for its exact<br/>identity claim value (e.g. preferred_username) --<br/>must be the SAME claim cert-issuer is<br/>configured to extract for this issuer, or the<br/>grant below will silently never match the<br/>token this user actually presents later
    activate IdP
    IdP-->>Admin: Exact claim value
    deactivate IdP

    Note over Admin,Graph: Repeatable. A signed admin action, the only way to grant or revoke<br/>(the unsigned credentials-grants and credentials-revocations topics were removed,<br/>docs/architecture/authority-model.md)

    Admin->>GrantTool: Run tool with arguments<br/>(grant: target_identity, permissions --<br/>or revoke: serial, reason)
    activate GrantTool
    GrantTool->>GrantTool: Sign the action with the admin's own<br/>certificate's key (SignedAdminAction:<br/>payload, author_serial, signature)
    GrantTool->>Cassini: Connect using the admin's own<br/>Polar client cert (mTLS)
    activate Cassini
    GrantTool->>Cassini: Publish the SignedAdminAction to<br/>credentials-admin-action-requests

    Cassini->>CredAgentCon: Deliver message
    activate CredAgentCon
    CredAgentCon->>CredAgentCon: Look the author's certificate up by serial in the ledger,<br/>refuse a revoked author, verify the signature,<br/>check the capability the action needs against the ledger record<br/>(never the certificate), refuse a replay by payload hash
    alt Refused
        CredAgentCon->>Cassini: Reply Refused (why) on<br/>credentials-admin-action-replies
    else Accepted
        CredAgentCon->>EventLog: Append AdminActionRecorded, fsync'd<br/>(hash includes previous entry's hash, the grant or<br/>revocation is derived from it in the state fold --<br/>a grant is later consumed by a matching issuance,<br/>never mutated or deleted here)
        activate EventLog
        EventLog-->>CredAgentCon: Appended
        deactivate EventLog
        CredAgentCon->>Graph: Project derived state<br/>(Grant node, or mark a<br/>Certificate node revoked --<br/>rebuildable from the event log,<br/>never the source of truth)
        activate Graph
        Graph-->>CredAgentCon: Written
        deactivate Graph
        CredAgentCon->>Cassini: Reply Recorded on<br/>credentials-admin-action-replies
    end
    deactivate CredAgentCon
    Cassini->>GrantTool: Deliver the reply
    deactivate Cassini
    GrantTool-->>Admin: Exit 0 only on Recorded
    deactivate GrantTool
